,572,7826,304,1059,13551,13,11201,11,279,54872,374,400,19,20,17,3,2889,54236,16217,11,323,29405,13166,429,1181,2608,12703,553,400,20,59,4,3,1449,1899,13,220,2585,16217,572,279,6008,400,17,3,5555,4134,979,1340,1156,13686,432,7826,30,17399,697,4226,438,264,12122,311,279,23480,55666,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nTwo weeks ago, Alice came home from vacation and noticed that a bean plant was growing in her garden. Today, the stalk is $452$ centimeters tall, and Alice observed that its height increases by $5\\%$ every day.  How tall was the plant $2$ weeks ago when she first noticed it growing? Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9ee1045d7be84623184b590889c00ffb0b0104bf7e340bef1ff367d532ff68cc"},"seconds":23.82227635383606,"seed":963327647730395201,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to work backwards from the current height of the plant to its height two weeks ago, considering that the height increases by $5\\%$ every day.\n\nLet's denote the height of the plant two weeks ago as $h$ centimeters. Since the plant grows by $5\\%$ each day, we can express its height each day as a multiple of its height from the previous day. Specifically, if the plant's height increases by $5\\%$ daily, then each day the height is multiplied by $1.05$ (since $100\\% + 5\\% = 105\\% = 1.05$).\n\nGiven that today the plant is $452$ centimeters tall and that two weeks (14 days) have passed, we can set up the following equation to represent the growth over those 14 days:\n\n\\[ h \\times (1.05)^{14} = 452 \\]\n\nTo find $h$, we need to solve for $h$:\n\n\\[ h = \\frac{452}{(1.05)^{14}} \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate $(1.05)^{14}$:\n\n\\[ (1.05)^{14} \\approx 1.979932 \\]\n\nNow, we can substitute this back into our equation for $h$:\n\n\\[ h = \\frac{452}{1.979932} \\]\n\nPerforming the division gives:\n\n\\[ h \\approx \\frac{452}{1.979932} \\approx 228.3 \\]\n\nTherefore, the height of the plant two weeks ago when Alice first noticed it growing was approximately $\\boxed{228.3}$ centimeters."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{228.3}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
